WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.730
A friend in Lyon texts you her plan:

2
00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:06.140
«Quand j'aurai dix-huit ans,
je voterai.» Word for word:

3
00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:07.940
when I will have eighteen years,

4
00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:09.120
I will vote.

5
00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:11.430
Two futures in one sentence.

6
00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:13.380
Then she adds: «Quand il pleut,

7
00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:15.790
je prends le bus.» Same «quand».

8
00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:17.600
This time, the present.

9
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:20.290
English says 'when I am eighteen'.

10
00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:23.440
So when does French choose
the future after 'when',

11
00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:25.060
and when doesn't it?

12
00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:27.880
In this mission, you'll build
'will' and 'would' from one

13
00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:29.910
stem in Mission D1.

14
00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:33.220
Then you'll pick the tense after
each conjunction in Mission I1,

15
00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:35.930
and watch it land on a timeline.

16
00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:40.420
Your mission: find out when
French says «quand» with a future,

17
00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:41.400
and when it doesn't.
